  "goodToKnow": "Der Skrupel is a scruple or qualm, mostly in the plural: keine Skrupel haben, moralische Skrupel. Skrupellos means unscrupulous: ein skrupelloser Geschäftsmann. It comes from Latin scrupulus, a small sharp stone, an image of something nagging the conscience. Synonyms: die Bedenken, die Gewissensbisse (pangs of conscience). The plural is the same: die Skrupel."
